<article class="env-variant" id="0699">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0699">Variant <span data-tag="0699">11.5.0.44</span>.</a> Let $\kappa \leq \lambda $ be regular cardinals. We say that $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ <em>admits $\lambda $-small $\kappa $-filtered colimits</em> if it admits $\operatorname{\mathcal{K}}$-indexed colimits, for every $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{K}}$ which is $\lambda $-small and $\kappa $-filtered. We say that a functor $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ <em>preserves $\lambda $-small $\kappa $-filtered colimits</em> if it preserves $\operatorname{\mathcal{K}}$-indexed colimits, for every $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{K}}$ which is $\lambda $-small and $\kappa $-filtered. </p>
