       where the horizontal maps are inner anodyne, $Y'$ is a Kan complex, and $f'$ is a Kan fibration. Then $f$ is $n$-connective if and only if $f'$ is $n$-connective, and $f$ is a weak homotopy equivalence if and only if $f'$ is a homotopy equivalence (Proposition <a data-tag="00UB" href="/tag/00UB">3.1.7.13</a>). The desired result now follows by applying Proposition <a data-tag="00X1" href="/tag/00X1">3.2.7.2</a> to the Kan fibration $f'$. 
